WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.085
Deception can have many goals,

00:00:02.085 --> 00:00:06.000
but from a defensive perspective the goals often cluster into a few useful categories.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.460
Some activity is meant to create urgency: act now, approve now, share now,

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.000
disable the control now.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.545
Some is meant to create confusion,

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:17.000
making the team spend time on the wrong claim or argue over incomplete context.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Some is meant to hide source, intent, or responsibility, so that a request, artifact,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
or narrative appears more trustworthy than it is.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Defensive signals are not proof.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.200
They are reasons to apply more care.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.000
Missing provenance, unusual urgency, unexplained gaps, selective screenshots,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.888
conflicting timestamps,

00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:36.725
and pressure to bypass normal process should all change how an analyst handles the

00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:37.000
claim.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.955
A single indicator may have an innocent explanation.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:42.200
A pattern of indicators may justify escalation, preservation,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.000
and independent corroboration.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.960
Selective evidence is especially important.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.000
A message thread can be cropped.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.985
A log line can be separated from surrounding events.

00:00:49.985 --> 00:00:51.520
A domain, file hash, username,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.000
or ticket number can be real while the conclusion attached to it is wrong.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The analyst should ask what is missing, what system of record can confirm the artifact,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
and whether the presented evidence supports the exact claim

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
or only a weaker version of it.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The purpose of naming signals is not to make teams suspicious of everything.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
It is to give them a repeatable way to move from reaction to verification.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
When urgency is high, process becomes more valuable, not less.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.095
Trusted channels, approval workflows, documented assumptions,

00:01:17.095 --> 00:01:21.050
and clear escalation paths help teams make timely decisions without giving pressure the

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.000
steering wheel.
